{"at":"2026-11-01T08:55:18.446Z","type":"command","sequence":4,"command":{"op":"click","selector":"text=How to Play","capture":"how-to-play"}}
{"at":"2026-11-01T08:55:18.600Z","type":"result","sequence":4,"path":"/Users/pelicannurse/.t3/projects/first-person-shooter-soul-game/docs/media/build30-review1/how-to-play.jpg","captureMs":116.70270800000071,"beforePause":{"phase":"dialog","dialog":"OPERATOR HANDBOOK\n×\nMOVE WITH PURPOSE.\nW A S D\nMove\nMOUSE\nLook\nLMB\nFire coil rifle\nRMB\nAim down sights\nR\nReload\nSHIFT\nSoul Shift / dash\nCTRL\nSprint\nSPACE\nJump\nHOLD E\nRecover nearby memory\nESC\nPause / release mouse\n\nSoul Shift protects briefly. Dash within 4.5 m of a charging enemy to cancel its shot and stagger it for 0.8 s. A blue emitter flash confirms the break. Dashing toward a charge stops early on a successful break so you can follow up. Sideways dodges retain full travel. It deals no damage; the 4.5 s cooldown still applies. Your shield regenerates when you avoid damage.\n\nTHREAT VISOR · Orange brackets beside an optic mean charging; muted brackets mean recent fire or hit. One lower readout identifies the eligible target nearest your aim, with a small retarget margin. Bearing chevrons combine all enemy types in a 30-degree sector: CHARGES counts charging enemies, SOURCES counts every eligible enemy there, including recent fire/hits. Charge warnings take priority over those histories. Type and individual histories are omitted only in bearing groups. Cues require clear optic line of sight, expire, and never show all enemies. The memory archive retains recovered stories when combat compacts their card.\n\nUNDERSTOOD\n↗"},"after":{"phase":"dialog","dialog":"OPERATOR HANDBOOK\n×\nMOVE WITH PURPOSE.\nW A S D\nMove\nMOUSE\nLook\nLMB\nFire coil rifle\nRMB\nAim down sights\nR\nReload\nSHIFT\nSoul Shift / dash\nCTRL\nSprint\nSPACE\nJump\nHOLD E\nRecover nearby memory\nESC\nPause / release mouse\n\nSoul Shift protects briefly. Dash within 4.5 m of a charging enemy to cancel its shot and stagger it for 0.8 s. A blue emitter flash confirms the break. Dashing toward a charge stops early on a successful break so you can follow up. Sideways dodges retain full travel. It deals no damage; the 4.5 s cooldown still applies. Your shield regenerates when you avoid damage.\n\nTHREAT VISOR · Orange brackets beside an optic mean charging; muted brackets mean recent fire or hit. One lower readout identifies the eligible target nearest your aim, with a small retarget margin. Bearing chevrons combine all enemy types in a 30-degree sector: CHARGES counts charging enemies, SOURCES counts every eligible enemy there, including recent fire/hits. Charge warnings take priority over those histories. Type and individual histories are omitted only in bearing groups. Cues require clear optic line of sight, expire, and never show all enemies. The memory archive retains recovered stories when combat compacts their card.\n\nUNDERSTOOD\n↗"},"clientMs":153.07958299999882,"pageErrors":[]}
